\ ==== instrument! ( value key instrument -- ), oscillator! ( value key oscillator instrument -- ) ====

\ instrument! changes one parameter of an instrument: its patch, for later
\ notes, and its sounding voices, which move to the new value in a straight
\ line over 64 frames (1.3 ms) rather than jumping. Keys: :level :pan
\ :cutoff :resonance :drive. oscillator! does the same for one oscillator's
\ :level :ratio or :width. instrument-patch! instead replaces the
\ instrument's patch for later notes only.

11 seed

: amp ( v hz -- a ) 48000 swap amplitude-at 0.70710678 / 1000 * round 1000 / ;
: left ( stereo -- v ) | stereo | stereo 0 stereo n-rows 0 1 submatrix ;
: right ( stereo -- v ) | stereo | stereo 0 stereo n-rows 1 2 submatrix ;
: begin-note ( patch -- ) silence-audio 0 instrument-patch! :a4 1 0 note-on 0.3 render-audio drop ;

\ === :level, ramped ===
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] } begin-note
0.25 :level 0 instrument! 0.5 render-audio to quieter
quieter 0 64 0 1 submatrix successive-differences abs max 0.1 < . cr   \ 1 (no step beyond a sine's own)
quieter 4800 24000 0 1 submatrix 1000 amp . cr                          \ 0.25
clear

\ === :pan ===
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] } begin-note
1 :pan 0 instrument! 0.5 render-audio to moved
moved left 1000 amp . moved right 1000 amp . cr                     \ 0 1.414 (the 64-frame ramp is too short to register)
0.2 render-audio to settled
settled left 1000 amp . settled right 1000 amp . cr                 \ 0 1.414 (right only)
clear

\ === :cutoff on a filtered saw, and on a patch without a filter ===
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw } ] :cutoff 5000 } begin-note
500 :cutoff 0 instrument! 0.5 render-audio to closed
closed 4800 24000 0 1 submatrix 3520 amp 0.001 < . cr               \ 1 (5 kHz to 500 Hz)
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw } ] } begin-note
500 :cutoff 0 instrument! 0.5 render-audio 4800 24000 0 1 submatrix 3520 amp 0.001 < . cr   \ 1 (the filter comes in)
clear

\ === oscillator! :ratio and :level ===
{ :oscillators [ { } ] } begin-note
2 :ratio 0 0 oscillator! 0.5 render-audio 4800 24000 0 1 submatrix to octave
octave 880 amp . octave 440 amp . cr                                \ 1 0
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } { :fixed-hz 100 } ] :modulation [ [ 1 0 2 ] ] } begin-note
0 :level 1 0 oscillator! 0.5 render-audio 4800 24000 0 1 submatrix 1100 amp . cr   \ 0 (the modulator silenced: no sidebands)
clear

\ === the patch keeps the change for the next note ===
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] } begin-note 0.5 :level 0 instrument! silence-audio
:a4 1 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio 4800 24000 0 1 submatrix 1000 amp . cr   \ 0.5
clear

\ === instrument-patch! leaves sounding notes alone ===
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1000 } ] } begin-note
{ :oscillators [ { :fixed-hz 1500 } ] } 0 instrument-patch! 0.5 render-audio to unchanged
unchanged left 1000 amp . unchanged left 1500 amp . cr               \ 1 0
:e5 1 0 note-on 0.5 render-audio 4800 24000 0 1 submatrix 1500 amp 0 > . cr   \ 1 (the next note has it)
silence-audio clear

\ errors
0.5 :glide 0 instrument!                            \ (not a live key)
2 :level 0 instrument!                              \ (level above 1)
0.5 "level" 0 instrument!                           \ (key not a symbol)
0.5 :level 16 instrument!                           \ (instrument out of range)
2 :ratio 8 0 oscillator!                            \ (oscillator out of range)
2 :detune 0 0 oscillator!                           \ (not a live key)
